          "distinct": true,
          "id": "2b705bcb81bc417e20d02f954882a6563fd2fc5a",
          "message": "fix(n3): a formula-level @forAll binds only in its formula (#6851)\n\n* fix(n3): a formula-level @forAll binds only in its formula\n\nA formula-level `@forAll :x` now reads each mention as `__uf.<n>.<iri>`, n being\nthe number of formula boundaries to the declaring formula (a de Bruijn index):\nunforgeable (a `.` cannot occur in a quickvar) and canonical (copies of one\nclosed formula are equal terms). A rule's premise-own universals become its\nmatching variables (`__up.`), its conclusion-own ones `__uc.` (asserted as\ndocument-level universals); every other formula-level universal matches only\nitself and is never substituted or captured. log:conclusion lifts a formula's\nown universals for its run. The writer declares each at the top of its formula.\n\nFixes #6754\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ScyGGohDhirnbLbrUSnA5n\n\n* fix(sparq-reason): premise universals match only stored ones; closures and writers keep formula scope\n\nReview round 1 on #6851:\n\n- A premise's own @forAll universal (`__up.`) is no longer a matching\n  variable that binds individual terms. It binds only a universal the\n  store holds, and two premise universals never bind the same one, so\n  `{ @forAll :x. :x :p :b } => ...` is not fired by the ground fact\n  `:c :p :b` but is fired by `@forAll :y. :y :p :b.` This matches EYE.\n  The compiled and counting engines refuse such a rule.\n- Universals that a rule's conclusion asserts during a log:conclusion /\n  log:supports run take that run's namespace and are restored into the\n  result formula as its own universals, not leaked as document-level.\n- Writers place each formula-level @forAll right before the first\n  statement that mentions it, and the scope check replays the parser\n  over that plan, so mid-formula declarations and an outer mention\n  before an inner redeclaration are written instead of refused.\n- CHANGELOG entry for the #6754 behaviour changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ScyGGohDhirnbLbrUSnA5n\n\n* fix(sparq-reason): reject universally quantified antecedents in every engine\n\nPremise-own @forAll (and scoped universals in containment/aggregation body patterns) are refused with one error by the naive, compiled and incremental engines; the premise-universal binding path is removed. Writer @forAll placement and quoted/conclusion universal scoping are kept.\n\n* fix(sparq-reason): check bound aggregation clauses; templates are values\n\nThe quantified-antecedent check saw only the clauses written in the rule\ntext. A log:forAllIn / log:collectAllIn clause reached through a variable\n(the subject, or a member of a written list) is now checked on its bound\nvalue just before evaluation, and refused with the same error, failing the\nrun. The check now covers only the matching clauses (collectAllIn's clause,\nboth forAllIn clauses), so a quantified collectAllIn template is collected\nas an ordinary quoted formula.\n\nThe parser sizes a formula-level universal's per-mention name from borrowed\ndata and charges it before building the term. A premise universal that\nreached a matcher past validation would match only itself (and stop a\ndebug build) instead of binding.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ScyGGohDhirnbLbrUSnA5n\n\n* fix(sparq-reason): check containment patterns bound through a variable\n\nA log:includes / log:notIncludes object that is a variable bound to a\nformula holding a formula-level universal is now refused with the\nquantified-antecedent error before matching, failing the run, as a written\nquantified pattern is. A bound pattern without one is not refused.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ScyGGohDhirnbLbrUSnA5n\n\n* fix(sparq-reason): scope parsed documents' universals; one clause/value quantifier walk\n\nA document parsed at run time (log:parsedAsN3, log:semantics) becomes a quoted\nformula, so its top-level @forAll now binds in that formula: the parser reads it\nwith a formula quantifier scope, giving the same term as the inline\n{ @forAll ... } spelling, and a parsed quantified formula bound as a clause or\npattern is rejected like the inline one.\n\nAntecedent-quantifier validation is now one recursive walk that tracks\nexecutable positions (premise, containment pattern, collectAllIn clause, both\nforAllIn clauses, at any nesting depth) apart from value positions (templates,\nscopes, other quoted formulas). validate_rule_quantifiers and the runtime checks\non bound clauses and patterns share it, so a template nested in another\naggregation's clause is accepted while a nested quantified clause is rejected.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ScyGGohDhirnbLbrUSnA5n\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
