          "distinct": true,
          "id": "5cfd3640a661d1bcaf994708f0d16a1e0c5adccc",
          "message": "fix(n3): returned formulas carry their bindings; unsound bound aggregation fails closed (#7161)\n\nBackward proofs now resolve a formula bound through a variable before matching, rename its free variables apart, and project answers through size-charged resolved substitution. Engine-minted names use a parser-illegal separator and are escaped by ownership on emission, so documents and stored data cannot capture a live application's variables. Alias-chain and depth exhaustion report a named refusal instead of dropping answers. Forward evaluation and the W3C N3 report are unchanged.\n\nAddresses #6943\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ScyGGohDhirnbLbrUSnA5n",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-03T01:20:24Z",
          "tree_id": "1317519a4e732eb1b07dac0b8142f18c5ac2150d",
